[{"id":"VRCE-6-43-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing Dhūmrākṣa slain, Rāvana-lord of the Raksasas-overwhelmed with a mighty rage, began to sigh like a serpent.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.478,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-53-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e4d71eac20bc2589ed06d27458705b5d9e9d6099795712331ca14b74823c21d8","compact":"04c1b86c375d0f36305b61721a9795b0b50b4a8154f6b7cd20711edcd8757c1a","nasal":"2d5066b95ceb1baa270b575631553995cfdd130b3fd129a6bfc82f49238f1822"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":2,"english":"Let invincible Rākşasas of dreadful prowess, march forth, placing before them Akampana, skilled in all weapons and arms.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9618958c0cc20c203e65cd1d765f7969235c2d2241b8df889901ed53167dfda3","compact":"447aec6420ec79202e3ffef3b9855acc4854d96d2eae1b4b65a6bac573fff4a7","nasal":"87d0e4b74661aee29cf35bfae1668d4cbd04f15ef9ec5b6a8660f384586e4dce"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":3,"english":"Then equipped with various arms, the foremost of Rākşasas, having dreadful eyes (in their heads, and of dreadful forms, marched forth, urged on by their general.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52212ce8d8c089021dfd6aa3f9bcae51674566095ebbd68ba64f73b241f25b92","compact":"8ea7dc6c51284fc69ce9306800de67400a3dd79fb9ff8b27515fcada57550493","nasal":"8ea7dc6c51284fc69ce9306800de67400a3dd79fb9ff8b27515fcada57550493"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":4,"english":"Ascending a large car, adorned with burnished gold, Akampana, possessed of the splendour of clouds,* and cloud-hued, and furnished with a voice resembling the roar of clouds, went out, environed by Rākașasas of terrific forms. *There is a pun here on the word Akampana-lit.one incapable of being shaken.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a68caca0b6c49c4787325ebf6bde36cc24afa8a1b1c2613e9654acae016c235f","compact":"8f012c0544a07914ca90c9a0f936181cb46d2deea901b56c44513f6efb4785c1","nasal":"035e1f5a8ee7a8058919be10d2f308fd6b61e5904bde5f72bb3faf4c260e452d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":5,"english":"Akampana, resembling the sun in power, was incapable of being shaken in fight by the very gods, and of being beheld by them. 1. Possessed of a person measuring, according to the commentator, a mass of clouds. I give the apparent sense, which answers. 2. Monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a9f5bcff71170b13aafcbc17a6d661a8f7e7800e30e9a9f171f36745d795cbb","compact":"d3b952718d3e4e852e50048af0845953504322f692713b9421efe08f104d8d31","nasal":"9c8c846b86607954ea676b9542d82b607619d9cb3a46c277b84000f6d96ffcbd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":6,"english":"And as, burning for battle, he rushed out in wrath, the steeds drawing his car suddenly lost their energy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8dd6cf14247d18e12ac2f539f578dc03c81e6a173a4e19ac60aabb36d5cc550d","compact":"65b60ad87739d283abdc0998efd22ea7a5381fc98fa89a3d267a23395e8eb739","nasal":"65b60ad87739d283abdc0998efd22ea7a5381fc98fa89a3d267a23395e8eb739"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":7,"english":"The left eye of that one delighting in encounter, began to throb. And his continence grew pale, and his voice faltered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.925,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90c5bdd339b68eacc66f8efc73fcd22789f0bde3c2fbe86d2c5f7edce4af492e","compact":"309fed31a1969c768ea7e13ae62ab50ad9e8753286a181c5116c2556623e5e4b","nasal":"1dde230d2bec21f427bfe39246e2c69b705cdfe023b1dcbfb0adf7fb7913cadc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":8,"english":"In a fair day, it looked foul with the wind breathing roughly. And fierce and frightful beasts and birds began to emit cries.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.565,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e97a50fadd9216c1379edf6e92a1d6a77c27f389fdebfc75d7e31a6978b20404","compact":"b31716a1569c4d2f6a77d1d4174bef580ab3550198ee0e24a8158876e305d2ea","nasal":"b31716a1569c4d2f6a77d1d4174bef580ab3550198ee0e24a8158876e305d2ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":9,"english":"That lion-shouldered one like a tiger in prowess, without heeding these ominous occurrences, marched forth into the field.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.984,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ea66eece214b47870f29d4638e26e71763a20a77cfc921718f49c4d3d722853","compact":"460e2c633df6cb2f0e033c11f17496b862fb1bc1a66495fa70194b0e4ec6f39d","nasal":"d4a0640e2920f1cd17dbed79c79f578393f48478c9c1aa226e5227a07524dfbb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":10,"english":"As that Rākşasa was setting out along with the Rākṣasas, he set up mighty roars as if agitating the deep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5656ba2090897446e34062219855a0b8f2f5dcc64de77649f94f11f5e1017c10","compact":"a25a90b69b47a60900350d779054ad898ed974c40e1e7ef90317820949260104","nasal":"c761a6d29be44a9966bce060308eb2eeb8343ee2a2d1d7b9393083a96ffdd34b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-43-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":43,"verse":11,"english":"The mighty army of monkeys was seized with trepidation at that sound. And then there took place a mighty encounter of the Rākṣasas and the monkeys equipped staying in fight with trees and rocks, who had given up all concern for their selves in behalf of Rāma and Rävaņa.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.509,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-55-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6043011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a51b2a2e6fc1d7c03e250ae111c6639ab69a6371ad94d1508391f64d115b6fb4","compact":"bfab08b1dd1457f5d3053f398d1172406dfaae859c8150cf0509560f0fb24951","n